menu "KilnCtrl Recovery"

    config KILNCTL_STAGE_CHIP_REV_CHECK
        bool "Check the image chip revision range when verifying a staged OTA image"
        default y
        help
            Build-time owner opt-out for RY-01. On: stage verify refuses an image whose
            header min/max chip revision excludes this chip (IDF
            bootloader_common_check_chip_validity) before anything is erased. Off: such an
            image passes the stage verify. In the recovery image the app partition is then
            erased and only the post-copy esp_image_verify refuses it, leaving the board
            in recovery with no app. Keep on unless you deliberately flash images built
            for a different chip revision. Not a runtime or web setting. The recovery
            image defines the same symbol (KilnFW_recovery/main/Kconfig.projbuild).

endmenu
